# Mosesploitable 1.0

Mosesploitable is an open-source Buildroot-based Linux system with a custom-compiled Linux kernel.

The project is focused on clarity, reproducibility, and control: a minimal but complete operating system that boots, runs, and can evolve across architectures.

---

## Name note

Mosesploitable is a project name chosen for personal preference.  
The system is not intentionally vulnerable.

---

## Project goals

- Build and maintain a real Linux system (kernel + userspace), not a demo
- Keep the setup clean, explicit, and understandable
- Support multiple architectures over time
- Serve as a solid base for experimentation, learning, and future evolution

This is NOT:

- a pre-made distribution copy
- a “just for fun” throwaway build
- a security challenge VM

---

## Current status

- Version: Mosesploitable 1.0
- Base: Buildroot (git snapshot)
- Kernel: Linux 6.18.2 (custom build)
- Primary architecture: x86_64
- Boot-tested: QEMU

The system boots successfully to login and provides a functional Linux environment.

---

## Build requirements

This project is intended to be built on a Linux environment.

Supported and tested build environments:

- Native Linux (recommended)
- Windows via WSL2 (tested with Ubuntu)

Building directly on Windows without WSL is not supported.

### Required tools and packages

A standard Linux build environment is required, including:

- GCC toolchain
- GNU Make
- Bash
- Git
- rsync
- cpio
- unzip
- patch
- bc
- Python 3

Buildroot will automatically build its own cross-compilers and host tools.

On Debian / Ubuntu systems, the following packages are typically required:

```bash
sudo apt install \
  build-essential \
  git \
  rsync \
  bc \
  unzip \
  cpio \
  python3 \
  file \
  wget
```

---

## Build system

The system is built using Buildroot, which handles:

- cross-compilation
- root filesystem generation
- kernel integration

Build artifacts are located in:

```
output/images/
 ├── bzImage
 ├── rootfs.ext2
 └── rootfs.tar
```

---

## Running with QEMU

### VGA mode

From any directory:

```bash
qemu-system-x86_64 \
  -kernel ~/buildroot/output/images/bzImage \
  -append "root=/dev/sda rw" \
  -hda ~/buildroot/output/images/rootfs.ext2 \
  -m 512
```

### Serial / headless mode

From any directory:

```bash
qemu-system-x86_64 \
  -kernel ~/buildroot/output/images/bzImage \
  -append "root=/dev/sda rw console=ttyS0" \
  -hda ~/buildroot/output/images/rootfs.ext2 \
  -nographic \
  -m 512
```

Default login (development setup):

- user: root
- password: root

---

## Roadmap

Planned evolution:

- additional architectures (ARM, i386, others)
- configuration cleanup and documentation
- clearer separation between Buildroot config and project identity

Buildroot is expected to remain the base up to version 2.0.  
Beyond that point, a transition to a full distribution base (e.g. Debian) may be evaluated.

---

## (MY) Philosophy

Buildroot is the tool.  
The system is ours.

Every choice is explicit. Every component is understood.  
No magic, no shortcuts.

